-- ============================================================================
-- Migration: Sheet Metal Machine Library (staging) -- part 1 of 4
-- Purpose: Lands the "machine_library" reference export (281 named real
--          machines across 15 categories: 2-Axis Router, 3/4 Roll Bender, 3D
--          Laser Cutting, Bend Press Brake, Laser Cutting, Fiber Laser
--          Cutting, CTL, Deslag, Laser Punch/Punch Press, Oxyfuel Cutting,
--          Waterjet Cutting, Turret Press, Progressive Die Press, Tandem
--          Press) into the same lossless staging table earlier migrations
--          created. See migration 479's header for the staging/promotion
--          architecture. Split into 4 files -- a single-file INSERT
--          of all 281 rows was too large for the Supabase SQL Editor (same
--          issue as migrations 493-498). Source scope is "World Average"
--          (NOT USA-specific like earlier categories) -- stored as
--          source_region='World Average' to avoid mislabeling world-average
--          rates as USA rates.
--
--          Sanitized of the licensed source's own name (its
--          source-name self-reference field, present on some rows, is
--          rewritten to a neutral label before storage) per the standing
--          rule against naming the licensed source.
--
--          One row per machine (key = "<category>:<machine name>"), full
--          spec preserved in `raw` (labor rates, cycle-time parameters,
--          physical envelope, power, price, location...). `value` holds
--          machine_price_usd (every row has one) as the closest thing to a
--          single representative scalar; the real content is in `raw`.
--
--          NOT promoted into any live table by this migration -- see
--          project memory for the specific, individually-justified
--          promotions this data enables.
-- Author: Principal Engineering Team
-- Date: 2026-08-20
-- Version: 1.0.0
-- ============================================================================

ON CONFLICT (category, source_region, source_version, key) DO NOTHING;
